---
/**
 * Said once on an English page whose long guide still comes from the French data (operator,
 * 2026-11-18: the interface is translated first). The French parts carry lang="fr" so a screen
 * reader switches voice; this note tells a sighted reader why the language changes. A page
 * whose French part is not a city guide passes its own sentence as the slot.
 */
---

<p class="french-note">
  <slot>The city guide below is written in French for now; an English version is coming.</slot>
</p>

<style>
  .french-note {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--thread-faint);
    color: var(--thread-dim);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
